CALSCALE:GREGORIAN
METHOD:PUBLISH
X-WR-CALNAME:The Sound of Music
X-WR-TIMEZONE:America/New_York
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Sound of Music
DTSTART:20270324T000000Z
DTEND:20270324T023000Z
DTSTAMP:20261118T003811Z
UID:1010415
DESCRIPTION:<p>For the first time in nearly three decades\, <em>The Sound 
 of Music</em> returns to Broadway\, directed by three-time Tony Award&reg\
 ; nominee Lear deBessonet\, Lincoln Center Theater&rsquo\;s Kewsong Lee Ar
 tistic Director (<em>Ragtime</em>\, 2026 Tony winner for Best Revival of a
  Musical\, <em>Into the Woods</em>) and choreographed by Tony winner Chris
 opher Gattelli (<em>Schmigadoon</em>). Featuring Rodgers &amp\; Hammerstei
 n&rsquo\;s unforgettable score\, including &ldquo\;Do-Re-Mi\,&rdquo\; &ldq
 uo\;My Favorite Things\,&rdquo\; &ldquo\;Edelweiss\,&rdquo\; and &ldquo\;C
 limb Ev&rsquo\;ry Mountain\,&rdquo\; and an iconic book written by Howard 
 Lindsay and Russell Crouse\, and starring Tony nominee Jasmine Amy Rogers 
 (<em>BOOP!</em>) as &ldquo\;Maria\," <em>The Sound of Music</em> returns a
 t a moment when humanity\, compassion\, and conviction feel vital and nece
 ssary.<br /><br />This revival finds new power in the intimate story of a 
 family learning to love again\, set against one of the most consequential 
 moments of the twentieth century\, as the Nazi regime rises to power and a
 uthoritarianism encroaches on daily life.</p>
LOCATION:Lincoln Center Theater-Vivian Beaumont\, 150 West 65th Street\, N
 ew York NY 10023
URL:https://www.telecharge.com/The-Sound-Of-Music-Tickets
END:VEVENT
